* START-HISTORY:
* 12 Nov 26 SD Core Solo - SOLO 62: the helper task is started by Task Scheduler COM; Start-ScheduledTask (CIM) is refused over ssh.
* 12 Nov 26 SD Core Solo - SOLO 62: a line before each wait (12982 before the report, about 8 s; 12981 before a change, up to 3 min
*           when ssh is set up): the owner, 12 Nov 26, "there needs to be a message to the user any time a command is expected to
*           take more than 2 seconds", after remote.ssh local sat silent for two minutes in the VM witness.
* 12 Nov 26 SD Core Solo - SOLO 62, first VM witness: the Solo folder is taken from the helper's own path (kernel(K$WINPATH)), not cut
*           from @sdsys, whose separators are mixed on Solo; the request is written to <Solo folder>\sdsys, where the helper reads it.
* 12 Nov 26 SD Core Solo - SOLO 62, new: Linux Solo's remotedoor (11 Nov 26, S.117) for Windows.  Linux Solo's doors are the
*           user's own systemd units, changed by tools/solo-service.sh with no sudo.  Windows Solo's are the API listener line in
*           sd.conf, the API firewall rule, Solo's own sshd (a SYSTEM task) and its firewall rule: machine objects a Solo session
*           cannot change.  So a change goes to the doors helper, gplbld/solo-doors.ps1, run as SYSTEM by the task "SD Core Solo
*           Doors" the installer registers (the owner, 12 Nov 26: option 2, "with the ability to manage remotely, not just console
*           only - by design solo is less secure than core"; "Set it up from the page" for ssh that was never set up).
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    REMOTE.API {OFF | LOCAL | OPEN}        the SD API, port 4249
*    REMOTE.SSH {OFF | LOCAL | OPEN}        Solo's own ssh server, port 4251
*       OFF     no listener (the API: APIPORT off in sd.conf; ssh: its task disabled and stopped)
*       LOCAL   it listens, and the firewall admits this computer only
*       OPEN    it listens, and the firewall admits other computers.  ON is taken as OPEN (SD Core's word).
*    With no keyword it reports the setting and changes nothing.
*
*    ADMINISTRATOR ONLY (ADMIN first), and a change asks for the administrator password AGAIN: the helper is a separate SYSTEM
*    process and believes a proof made from the password, not this session's flag.  The proof is SCRAM's ClientProof over
*    'sd-solo-doors|v1|door|mode|nonce|time', made here from the $ADMIN (or, in managed mode, $GLOBAL) record of $cred and
*    checked by the helper against the same record's StoredKey; solo-doors.ps1's header has the exact form.  THE LIMIT, which the
*    owner accepted (12 Nov 26, "i"): $cred is in the user's own folder, so the proof stops a request made without the password,
*    not a program running as this user.
*
*    THE REPORT IS WHAT IS INSTALLED, NOT WHAT WAS ASKED: solo-doors.ps1 -Show, unelevated, reads sd.conf, the two firewall rules
*    (through their scripts' -ScopeFile verdicts) and the ssh task, and says whether each port listens now.
*    A CHANGE SUCCEEDS ONLY ON THE HELPER'S OWN LINE "SOLO API LISTENER <mode>" or "SOLO SSH LISTENER <mode>", in the answer whose
*    first line names this request's nonce - never on an exit status, and never on an older answer.
*    THE API LISTENER ONLY MOVES WHEN SD NEXT STARTS (sd-solo -stop, then sd-solo -start, or the next boot): the helper does not
*    restart SD, which would end every session, a remote caller's included.  The verb says so when the listener setting moved.
*    WHAT REACHES A COMMAND LINE: the helper's path and the Solo folder (this SD's own), refused if either holds a single quote.
*    Nothing a person typed: door and mode are this program's words, and the request travels in a file.
*    A change is audited here (remote.api mode=open status=ok | refused) and in the helper's own log.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
program remote.door
$catalog $remotedoor

$include int$keys.h
$include keys.h
$include err.h

deffun ps_script_out(script, want.out) calling '!ps_script_out'

   prompt ''
   @system.return.code = -ER$ARGS

   if not(kernel(K$ADMINISTRATOR, -1)) then
      stop sysmsg(2001) ;* Command requires administrator privileges
   end

   words = trim(downcase(@sentence))
   verb = field(words, ' ', 1)
   begin case
      case verb = 'remote.api'
         door = 'api' ; dname = 'The API' ; port = 4249 ; anchor = 'SOLO API LISTENER '
      case verb = 'remote.ssh'
         door = 'ssh' ; dname = 'ssh' ; port = 4251 ; anchor = 'SOLO SSH LISTENER '
      case 1
         stop sysmsg(15971, 'remote.api')                         ;* the program was reached by another word: say how it is used
   end case

   nw = dcount(words, ' ')
   want = ''
   if nw > 2 then stop sysmsg(15971, verb)                        ;* %1 off | local | open
   if nw = 2 then
      want = field(words, ' ', 2)
      if want = 'on' then want = 'open'
      if want # 'off' and want # 'local' and want # 'open' then stop sysmsg(15971, verb)
   end

*  The Solo folder is the folder of the helper, which the installer puts in it (as apisrvr finds solo-sshkey.ps1).  12 Nov 26: it was cut
*  from @sdsys at its last @ds, but Solo's paths are built with mixed separators (sd.conf has no SDSYS line; config.c makes it), so
*  no @ds was found and the helper was handed an empty folder ("no -AppDir, or it has no sdsys folder", the first VM witness).
   script = kernel(K$WINPATH, '/solo-doors.ps1')
   tail = '\solo-doors.ps1'
   if downcase(script[len(script) - len(tail) + 1, len(tail)]) # tail then stop sysmsg(15966, 'the helper path is not one this verb understands: ' : script)
   app.dir = script[1, len(script) - len(tail)]
   if index(script : app.dir, "'", 1) then stop sysmsg(15966, 'the Solo folder has a single quote in its name')

   gosub show
   if not(rep.read) then
      @system.return.code = -ER$FAILED
      stop
   end

   if want # '' then
      if not(helper.ok) then
         void kernel(K$AUDIT, verb : ' mode=' : want : ' status=refused reason=no helper')
         @system.return.code = -ER$FAILED
         stop sysmsg(12985)                                       ;* The doors helper is not installed on this computer ...
      end
      gosub change
      if not(done) then
         @system.return.code = -ER$FAILED
         gosub show
         stop
      end
      gosub show
   end

   gosub report
   if rep.ok then @system.return.code = 0 else @system.return.code = -ER$FAILED
   stop

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- solo-doors.ps1 -Show.  Out: rep.read, mode, listening, helper.ok, doors.dir
show:
   rep.read = @false
   ps = "& '" : script : "' -Show -AppDir '" : app.dir : "'"
   ps := @fm : 'exit $LASTEXITCODE'
   display sysmsg(12982)                                          ;* Reading the doors (a few seconds)...  (owner, 12 Nov 26: say so before any wait over 2 s)
   both = ps_script_out(ps, @true)
   rc = field(both, @fm, 1)
   out = field(both, @fm, 2, 99999)
   mode = '' ; listening = '' ; helper.ok = @false ; doors.dir = '' ; lastl = ''
   for i = 1 to dcount(out, @fm)
      ln = trim(out<i>)
      if ln # '' then lastl = ln
      key = trim(field(ln, ':', 1))
      val = trim(ln[index(ln, ':', 1) + 1, 99999])
      if key = door : ' mode' then mode = val
      if key = door : ' listening' then listening = val
      if key = 'doors helper' then helper.ok = (val = 'yes')
      if key = 'doors dir' then doors.dir = val
   next i
   if rc # 0 or mode = '' then
      if lastl = '' then lastl = 'the helper gave no answer (status ' : rc : ')'
      display sysmsg(15966, lastl)                                ;* The setting could not be read: %1
      return
   end
   rep.read = @true
   return

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- what is installed, in words.  Out: rep.ok
report:
   rep.ok = @true
   begin case
      case mode = 'off'
         display sysmsg(15970, dname)                             ;* %1 is off: SD has no listener for it
      case mode = 'notsetup'
         display sysmsg(12984)                                    ;* ssh is not set up on this computer ...
      case mode = 'local'
         display sysmsg(15969, dname, port)                       ;* %1 is local: only this computer can connect (port %2)
      case mode = 'open'
         display sysmsg(15968, dname, port)                       ;* %1 is open: other computers can connect (port %2)
      case 1
         display sysmsg(15966, mode)
         rep.ok = @false
         return
   end case
   if (mode = 'local' or mode = 'open') and listening # 'yes' then
      display sysmsg(15965, port)                                 ;* ...but nothing listens on port %1 now
      rep.ok = @false
   end
   return

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- one change through the helper.  Out: done
change:
   done = @false

*  The password, again, and which record it opens: the administrator's, or in managed mode the global one (as ADMIN tries them).
   display sysmsg(12002) : ' ' :                                  ;* Administrator password:
   input pw HIDDEN
   cred = ''
   ok = @false
   call !CRED_VERIFY('$ADMIN', pw, ok)
   if ok then cred = '$ADMIN'
   if not(ok) then
      call !CRED_VERIFY('$GLOBAL', pw, ok)
      if ok then cred = '$GLOBAL'
   end
   if cred = '' then
      pw = ''
      sleep 2
      void kernel(K$AUDIT, verb : ' mode=' : want : ' status=refused reason=wrong password')
      display sysmsg(12987)                                       ;* Wrong password - nothing was changed
      return
   end

*  ClientKey from the password and the record's salt, then the proof over this request.  The password goes no further.
   openpath @sdsys : @ds : '$cred' to cred.f else
      pw = ''
      display sysmsg(15966, '$cred could not be opened')
      return
   end
   read cred.rec from cred.f, cred else cred.rec = ''
   close cred.f
   salt = cred.rec<CRED$SALT> ; iter = cred.rec<CRED$ITER> ; stored.key = cred.rec<CRED$STOREDKEY>
   salted = SDEXT(pw : @FM : salt : @FM : iter : @FM : SCRAM$KEY.LEN, @TRUE, SD_PBKDF2)
   pw = ''
   client.key = SDEXT(salted : @FM : 'Client Key', @TRUE, SD_HMACSHA256)
   salted = ''
   nonce = ''
   call !SD_GET_SALT(nonce)
   now = (date() - 732) * 86400 + int(time())                     ;* LOCAL seconds since 1 Jan 1970: day 732 is that date
   authmsg = 'sd-solo-doors|v1|' : door : '|' : want : '|' : nonce : '|' : now
   sig = SDEXT(stored.key : @FM : authmsg, @TRUE, SD_HMACSHA256)
   proof = SDEXT(client.key : @FM : sig, @TRUE, SD_XORBYTES)
   client.key = ''
   if nonce = '' or sig = '' or proof = '' then
      display sysmsg(15966, 'the request could not be signed')
      return
   end

*  The request, the task and the wait, in ONE PowerShell script run as this user (!ps_script_out).  Not OSWRITE and OSREAD: those are
*  !oswrite and !osread, ordinary programs that ask the account's OS switch, which is off as delivered, and the answer is in
*  %ProgramData%.  Every value put in the script is base64, a number, a word of this program, '$ADMIN' / '$GLOBAL' or a path of this
*  SD's own (checked above for a single quote), each inside single quotes, where PowerShell expands nothing.  The answer is
*  result.txt in the helper's folder, whose first line names THIS request's nonce; setting ssh up can take a minute, so it waits 180 s.
   q = char(39)
   ps = '$req = (' : q : 'version=1' : q : ', ' : q : 'door=' : door : q : ', ' : q : 'mode=' : want : q : ', ' : q : 'nonce=' : nonce : q
   ps := ', ' : q : 'time=' : now : q : ', ' : q : 'cred=' : cred : q : ', ' : q : 'proof=' : proof : q : ') -join "`n"'
   ps<-1> = '[IO.File]::WriteAllText(' : q : app.dir : '\sdsys\doors.request' : q : ', $req + "`n", [Text.Encoding]::ASCII)'   ;* where the helper reads it (Join-Path -AppDir sdsys)
*  The task is started through the Task Scheduler's COM object, not Start-ScheduledTask: that is a CIM cmdlet, and in an ssh logon
*  every CIM cmdlet fails ("Cannot connect to CIM server. Access denied", the VM witness of 12 Nov 26).
   ps<-1> = 'try { $ts = New-Object -ComObject Schedule.Service; $ts.Connect(); $null = $ts.GetFolder(' : q : '\' : q : ').GetTask(' : q : 'SD Core Solo Doors' : q : ').Run($null) } catch { Write-Output ("cannot start the helper: " + $_.Exception.Message); exit 4 }'
   ps<-1> = '$res = ' : q : doors.dir : '\result.txt' : q
   ps<-1> = 'for ($i = 0; $i -lt 180; $i++) {'
   ps<-1> = '   Start-Sleep -Seconds 1'
   ps<-1> = '   if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $res) {'
   ps<-1> = '      $l = @([IO.File]::ReadAllLines($res))'
   ps<-1> = '      if ($l.Count -gt 0 -and $l[0] -eq ' : q : 'nonce=' : nonce : q : ') { $l | ForEach-Object { Write-Output $_ }; exit 0 }'
   ps<-1> = '   }'
   ps<-1> = '}'
   ps<-1> = 'exit 3'
   display sysmsg(12981)                                          ;* The doors helper is making the change: ... (owner, 12 Nov 26: say so before any wait over 2 s)
   both = ps_script_out(ps, @true)
   rc = field(both, @fm, 1)
   answer = field(both, @fm, 2, 99999)
   if rc = 4 then
      void kernel(K$AUDIT, verb : ' mode=' : want : ' status=refused reason=the helper task could not be started')
      display sysmsg(15967, dname, trim(answer<1>))               ;* %1 was not changed: %2
      return
   end
   if rc # 0 then
      void kernel(K$AUDIT, verb : ' mode=' : want : ' status=refused reason=no answer')
      display sysmsg(12986, 180)                                  ;* The doors helper gave no answer within %1 seconds
      return
   end

   lastl = ''
   next.start = @false
   n = dcount(answer, @fm)
   for i = 2 to n
      ln = trim(answer<i>)
      if ln = anchor : want then done = @true
      if ln[1, 10] = 'NEXT START' then next.start = @true
      if ln[1, 8] = 'REFUSED:' or index(ln, 'FAIL', 1) then lastl = ln
   next i
   if not(done) then
      void kernel(K$AUDIT, verb : ' mode=' : want : ' status=refused')
      if lastl = '' then lastl = 'the helper did not confirm the change'
      display sysmsg(15967, dname, lastl)                         ;* %1 was not changed: %2
      return
   end
   void kernel(K$AUDIT, verb : ' mode=' : want : ' status=ok')
   if next.start then display sysmsg(12983)                       ;* The API listener changes when SD is next started ...
   return

end

* END-CODE
